   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the retirement and social security law, in relation to\ntransfer of retirement membership for certain employees of SUNY within the\nprofessional, scientific and technical bargaining unit",
    "basePrintNo": "S8959",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8959-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §618, R & SS L",
    "lawSection": "Retirement and Social Security Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8959\n\nSPONSOR: SAVINO\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the retirement and social security law, in relation to\ntransfer of retirement membership for certain employees of SUNY within\nthe professional, scientific and technical bargaining unit\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo allow certain employees, who are participants in the Optional Retire-\nment Program (ORP) established pursuant to article 8-b of the New York\nState Education Law, to join the New York State and Local Retirement\nSystem (ERS) or the New York State Teachers Retirement System (IRS) and\nto purchase credit for past service accrued while participating in the\nORP.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 of the bill defined an \"eligible employee\" as an individual\nwho, as of the effective date of this Act, is an active employee of the\nState University of New York (SUNY) in the professional, scientific and\ntechnical bargaining unit, a participant in the ORP, who is a registered\nnurse first employed of SUNY Stony Brook Hospital between the dates\nJanuary 1, 1996 and December 31, 1999, and as of the date of their\ntransfer application, is still an active SUNY employee. Such eligible\nemployees must submit an application for membership in ERS or TRS no\nlater than December 31, 2020.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe SUNY Optional Retirement Program is a defined contribution plan and\nwas established in 1964 as an alternative retirement option to member-\nship in ERS and TRS. All full-time employees in the unclassified service\nare eligible to participate in the optional plan; should a member fail\nto elect participation, they are be automatically placed in ERS or TRS\ndepending on title.\n\nUnder current law, should an optional plan participant leave SUNY,\ncommence employment with another New York State agency, and thus become\na member of ERS or TRS, they will not be permitted to establish credit\nfor any service for which the state contributions under the optional\nplan were made on their behalf. This bill would allow individuals to\nboth apply for membership in ERS and/or TRS and to purchase past-service\ncredit for the period of time the eligible employee participated in the\nORP.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2019 Session - S6110 - vetoed by Governor - Veto Message 283\n\n2018 Session - S6435-B (Flanagan) - vetoed by Governor - Veto Message\n286\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nIf this bill is enacted, the number of employees who may be affected\ncannot be readily determined. For every employee who does so elect,\nthere will be an annual cost to the State of New York of approximately\n13% of salary beginning with the fiscal year ending March 31, 2023.  In\naddition to the annual cost above, for every member who elects this\nbenefit, there will be a past service cost that will depend on the age,\nservice and salary of the member. Members will be able to pay this cost\nusing any of three methods, including a transfer of funds from their\nOptional Retirement Program balance, a one-time payment, or by payroll\ndeduction over a period not to exceed five (5) years.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n",
